# Spotify Playback Fix Walkthrough

I have addressed the issue where the Spotify player wasn't updating even when music was playing.

## Changes Made

### 'Play Here' Integration
- Added a **"Play Here"** button directly onto the vinyl record when the player is connected but idle.
- Clicking this button (or the record itself) will trigger a **playback transfer** to the CraftCanvas player. This is a crucial step for the Spotify Web Playback SDK to take control and start reporting the playback state.
- Once clicked, Spotify will move its active session to the browser, the record will start spinning, and the track info will appear.

### Improved Status Messaging
- Updated the placeholder text:
  - **"Connecting..."** while the SDK initializes.
  - **"Ready to Play"** once the device is registered but idle.
  - **"Press 'Play Here' or start music on Spotify"** as a helpful instruction for the user.

## Verification

### Manual Verification Steps
- [ ] Load the dashboard: See "Ready to Play" on the static vinyl.
- [ ] Hover over the record and click **"Play Here"**.
- [ ] Verify that music starts playing (if a session was active) or that the player becomes the active Spotify device.
- [ ] Observe the vinyl spinning and track details appearing once playback is active.
